# OpenCode dispatch

For OpenCode worker assignments only; native codex/* and claude/* aliases must
never reach oc.sh. Verify exact generated agents' discovery/resolved permissions
live; legacy permission syntax remains unchanged pending separate investigation.
Model catalog resolution alone is not enforcement or served model identity.

Write prompt before dispatch. Example first builder attempt (use the assigned
role/model/pass, not these paths on a rerun):

```bash
.agent-pipeline/bin/oc.sh --agent builder --model __BUILDER_MODEL__ --text \
  --prompt-file .agent-pipeline/prompts/T-<id>/builder-1.md \
  --raw-out .agent-pipeline/logs/T-<id>/builder-1.jsonl
```

Prompt includes task id, role, assigned patch for implementation, baseline, and
specific outstanding work, not leader instructions. First call omits --session;
record `oc.sh: session=ses_...` in the implementer/reviewer/tester role row on
any outcome. Later calls use only that task/role/model session after inactivity
is confirmed. Do not use --fork. Session receipts are not completion evidence.
Always --text; raw-out is immutable diagnostic evidence, not a lead input.

--auto is off unless approved and recorded OpenCode auto mode: on for this task;
only builder calls may use it. Never reviewer, tester, lead, or timeout recovery.
It can auto-approve non-denied commands; do not claim denies work until verified
live with the exact generated artifact and explicit consent for auto-mode tests.

Prefer host background execution/completion notifications. If unavailable:

```bash
.agent-pipeline/bin/bg-dispatch.sh start T-<id> builder-1 -- .agent-pipeline/bin/oc.sh \
  --agent builder --model __BUILDER_MODEL__ --text \
  --prompt-file .agent-pipeline/prompts/T-<id>/builder-1.md \
  --raw-out .agent-pipeline/logs/T-<id>/builder-1.jsonl
.agent-pipeline/bin/bg-dispatch.sh wait T-<id> builder-1 30
```

Link the .dispatch/ directory. Wait uses actual wrapper exit status: 0 success,
2 failed/unknown, 3 running. On 3 wait in bounded slices, never replace; on 2
inspect saved stderr and confirm authenticated server-side inactivity first.
Timeout (124)/killed wrapper cancellation is best-effort; unknown activity blocks
redispatch. No automatic retries or model substitutions. Report quota/permission
failure immediately; scheduled retry needs authorization and an actual scheduler.
